; refusal-nonfinite-expr: two domain failures with the same contract. `sqrt`
; of a negative is NaN, and `pow 10 400` is +infinity; neither is a finite
; f32, so the compile dry-run refuses both tracks. The diagnostics collect,
; so one score can show both at once.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4])

(track :target nan :expr (sqrt -1))
(track :target inf :expr (pow 10 400))
